phase P21
title Runtime ownership repair

tasks
    T200
        title        P00 — Adopt the reviewed Phase 2.1 preparation baseline
        status       done
        priority     high
        derives_from [@plan.Verification.D1, @plan.Verification.C1, @plan.Verification.V8]
        description
            Source Bead flow-state-e7p.13.0 (closed).
            Deliverable: adopt the reviewed preparation snapshot as a reproducible
            starting point; it is evidence, not runtime implementation.
            Allowed paths: only the preparation files listed in the source Bead
            handoff. Keep contracts, frozen code, generated output, and unrelated work
            outside scope.
        acceptance
            - The preparation boundary and exact diff are recorded with the source
              checks.
            - Independent review receipts passed at adoption; this does not claim
              runtime behavior.
            - Evidence: source Bead handoff, preparation diff, and check receipts.

    T201
        title        P01 — Adopt preparation and prove stable-admission waiter interruption
        status       done
        priority     high
        derives_from [@plan.Runtime.D1, @plan.Runtime.C1, @plan.Runtime.V3]
        description
            Source Bead flow-state-e7p.13.14 (closed).
            Deliverable: prove that interrupting one stable-admission follower leaves
            the leader running and able to admit exactly once.
            Allowed paths: packages/flow-state-rewrite/src/runtime/runtime.ts and its
            runtime integration tests.
        acceptance
            - The follower observes interruption while the same-ref leader succeeds
              once.
            - Lookup returns the leader's actor and runtime close succeeds.
            - Evidence: assembled admission-path proof and same-snapshot architecture,
              contract, and bug reviews.

